Per Apache License 2.0 Section 4, this NOTICE documents that files from the
original source have been modified. Summary of modifications made by
SDeVPro:

  - Product identity, CLI branding, documentation, default assets
    (including logo), directory layout, internal module paths, and build
    tooling (PyInstaller spec, Go sidecar naming, install/build scripts,
    CI workflow) rebranded and renamed throughout from "Strix" to
    "SDeVPro". The original multi-agent engine now lives at
    `sdevpro/engine/` (import path `sdevpro.engine.*`) as an internal,
    nested subpackage of the single top-level `sdevpro` package, rather
    than a separate top-level "strix" package.
  - Outbound product telemetry/analytics (PostHog and Scarf event
    reporting) and the automatic self-update / update-notification
    mechanism permanently disabled and stripped of their endpoints and
    API keys, so no scan or usage data is sent to any third-party service
    and the running build can never be silently replaced by a
    third-party release.
  - Added a new, independent scanning/reporting engine (the top-level
    `sdevpro` package: `sdevpro/scanner/`, `sdevpro/ai_analyst.py`,
    `sdevpro/reporter.py`, `sdevpro/log_analyzer.py`, `sdevpro/github_scan.py`)
    that runs security assessments natively without a Docker runtime,
    intended for local/on-premise or serverless deployment.
  - Added a Telegram bot interface (`sdevpro.telegram_bot`) — Uzbek/
    Russian/English UI, per-user encrypted AI (LLM) API keys, GitHub
    repository scanning, scheduled recurring scans, and server-log
    attack-source analysis, with PDF/TXT report export.
  - Added a Flask-based webhook adapter (`sdevpro/webhook_app.py`,
    `api/index.py`, `vercel.json`) for serverless (e.g. Vercel)
    deployment, with a pluggable storage backend (local JSON files or
    Upstash Redis).
  - The nested `sdevpro/engine/` package (the original multi-agent,
    Docker-sandboxed pentesting core) is kept for reference/advanced use
    and is otherwise functionally unmodified beyond the renaming,
    branding, and telemetry/self-update changes noted above — it makes no
    network connection to any third-party "Strix" service.

